WEBVTT

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.570
This is goodbye, Musashi.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.430
I'm going to resume my rest within you.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.030
<b>What's in a Katana</b>

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.080
Listen well.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:14.990
No matter what foes you face, 
you must not die.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.910
Because you are my vessel.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.960
And because Jisai was killed before 
we could finish what we started.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.040
Jisai? You mean Pops?

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.660
What's he got to do with this?

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.870
There's no time.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.870
I shall borrow your body.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.090
What are you gonna do?

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.190
Witness my last fight in the material world.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.120
I'm going to dispose of the 
enemy with a single blow!

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.190
It's drawing energy from
 every Kitetsu Blade here...

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.660
There's only one person who could do that!

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.750
See?! My goddess is the real deal!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.210
I will <i>never</i> be yours.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.210
Aw, you're gonna hurt my feelings!

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:39.920
This is goodbye.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.420
Until we meet again.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.260
What happened?

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.840
Amazing!

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.800
It was over in an instant...

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.950
Where's the enemy?

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.050
Gone.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.480
Did we really manage to survive...?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.060
All thanks to that boy.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.850
<i>I can still feel the sensation 
throughout my body...</i>

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:46.110
<i>My heart is pounding.</i>

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.240
<i>She was incredible.</i>

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.130
<i>And we were able to survive with her help!</i>

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.660
Musashi!

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.250
You two are okay! What a relief!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.030
How are you? Anything feel funny?

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.420
Musashi, you were awesome!

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.760
What even was that?! 
It was crazy strong!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.970
You beat the enemy with one attack!

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.340
Well, to be honest, that wasn't really me.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.520
I could tell.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.530
You seemed like a totally different person.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:16.330
Yeah! It was so weird!

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:19.180
Were you possessed by a ghost or 
something? Like an evil spirit?

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.150
Hey! Don't talk about her like that.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:26.100
She seemed really nice, 
and she was worried about Musashi.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.600
What is it, Tsugumi?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:34.250
Kojiro... are you the type to trust 
any girl who's a little nice to you?

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.810
You didn't learn your lesson after I
kicked your butt when we first met?

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.990
I'm worried about your future...

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.410
Wh-What's wrong with my future?!

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.990
Shut up! And what's so bad about it?!

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.920
<i>She did save us, but...</i>

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:54.420
<i>Jisai was killed before we 
could finish what we started.</i>

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:57.700
<i>What was she talking about?</i>

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:02.160
<i>Does that lady know Pops somehow?</i>

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:06.130
Hey, Musashi, what's up with that sword?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.120
This sword?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.030
It broke!

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.080
Seriously?! Again?!

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.830
A Kitetsu Blade shatters if it channels 
more power than it can contain.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.390
The blacksmith!

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:20.520
In other words, that katana breaking 
is a sign of your potential.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.930
Your last attack was really something!

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.880
You saved all our tails.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.570
If there's anything you'd like as thanks,
 just let us know.

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:34.890
We could choose a new katana for you!

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.210
I'll even hone it!

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.430
Why do you get to do that?

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.860
Gotta get in early with
 someone this promising!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.610
Imagine what it'd do for 
your rep and your blades!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.570
What in the world?!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.420
This giant hole wasn't here before, was it?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:54.030
Isn't this where the Kishin's body was? 
Where'd it go?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.350
Well, that was dangerous.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.900
We managed to escape thanks 
to your technique, Master.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:38.100
But we finally found the obsidian goddess.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.950
She's not getting away next time.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.090
What a sight...

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.440
A lot of Bushi did die yesterday.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:12.820
Is this... like a funeral?

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:36.450
This is how Bushi pay their respects, huh?

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:41.360
Father... Mother...

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.900
Father! Mother!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.820
No one wants to walk away from the swords.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.250
Yeah. They're mementos, after all.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.330
Kitetsu Blades are kinda special, y'know?

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:04.400
The feelings of their wielders 
linger inside of them.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:12.330
Some people treat them 
like the symbol of a Bushi's life.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.340
Our katanas...

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.650
My dad said something similar once.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:27.360
Well, I can't say I really agree with it.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.360
What do you mean, Tsugumi?

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.320
My blades belonged to my late sister.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:39.560
But they're just objects.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:42.360
They're no replacement for her.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.750
When someone dies, it's all over.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.710
They're gone and won't be coming back.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.180
Tsugumi...

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:03.510
Or whatever!

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:04.100
Ow!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.630
What was that for?!

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:09.190
And here I thought you had a little depth!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.920
<b>Ryuzoji
Band</b>

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.920
<b>Ryuzoji
Band</b>

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:31.750
Hooray! First futon in ages!

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.490
So you'll be taking off tomorrow?

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.270
Roll-a-roll-a-roll-a-roll!

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:34.610
So fluffy!

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:34.290
Right.

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.130
The Kishin's gone, after all.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:37.510
I can't believe how fluffy these are!

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.900
Thanks for putting us up for the night.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.480
We're not sleeping outside for once!

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.260
Thanks for saving our lives.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.770
See you.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:44.840
Hang on!

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.920
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:50.470
What's this all about?

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:09.750
<b>R
y
u
z
o
u
j
i

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:07.270
This young man will now attempt 
his sword trial again.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.610
He's trying again!

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.920
This is what he asked for?

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.660
It's that redhead. 
I hope it goes well for him this time!

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.300
He failed his first try, right?

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.960
Is this gonna work? Didn't he give 
off that black shine last time?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.320
<i>I need to return to sleep soon.</i>

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:40.290
<i>When I do, Musashi will 
lose the obsidian power...</i>

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:45.150
He's not gonna have that dark glow again.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:48.550
It's gotta be okay this time!

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:51.620
Huh?

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.120
That sword...

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:01.640
It's the same red blade 
he failed with the first time!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.770
Why would he choose that?!

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:05.560
Talk about bad luck!

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:09.020
It's the best one we have 
on hand at the moment.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.830
Listen up. The trial is the same as before.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:16.200
If the Kitetsu Blade glows, you pass.
 If it doesn't, you fail.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:18.750
You get one shot at this.
There are no do-overs.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:20.240
Understood?

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:21.800
Yeah!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.580
Hey, Tsugumi.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.790
Huh? What is it?

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:37.780
Remember what you said about katana 
being the symbols of a Bushi's life?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.270
To be honest, I don't know 
what to believe either.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:04.410
This is bad! Why's he bringing that up now?

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.240
But y'know...

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:12.770
Pops cared a lot about swords
and the Bushi way.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:17.770
<i>You swear loyalty to whatever you 
cherish and gives you strength,</i>

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.460
<i>then live without ever betraying that.</i>

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:22.560
<i>That's the Bushi way of life.</i>

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:26.520
So I want to learn more about them.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.960
Where will the road lead me 
once I take up my katana?

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.690
What's the world of Bushi like?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:45.810
It's true that the dead are gone forever.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.090
But the things that they cared about...

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:54.740
If I'm still here and
 able to cherish them too...

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:00.750
Then isn't there still something to symbolize

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.040
that they were once alive?

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:21.980
And so...

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:40.490
It lit up!

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:54.810
The sword trial for
 Enma's Oodachi is a success!

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:02.850
You did it, Musashi!

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.370
Musashi! You can finally use one, too!

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.110
Kojiro!

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:19.530
Now we can finally fight side-by-side—

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.470
This is great, Red! You did it!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.310
What gives?

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.960
Making a big fuss, aren't we?

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:34.290
Nobody seemed to care when <i>I</i> passed.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:35.760
That's just how it is.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:38.890
Your soul was blue, remember?

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.780
Yeah, and?

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:44.270
Get a load of Musashi's color.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.680
His color?

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:47.720
Looks red.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.910
Yep. A burning bright red.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.450
Remember what we learned?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.640
About the color of a Bushi's soul?

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.140
<i>There are five colors in total.</i>

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:02.880
<i>And depending on the color, 
a Kitetsu Blade can use different powers.</i>

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.480
So blue is average?

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:08.830
Yep! Blue's a totally normal color that 
about half all Bushi are born with.

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:13.260
Compared to that, only a few Bushi are red!

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.310
It's rare and powerful.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.880
He got the rare and powerful one?!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:22.190
That's a great color 
you've got there, Musashi!

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.670
Aw...

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.730
This is worth celebrating, Red!

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.560
Nicely done.

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:29.740
Everyone's fawning over Musashi...

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:33.770
I completed my trial 
two days sooner than he did!

00:15:33.770 --> 00:15:37.860
I can tell Kojiro's sulking because 
he feels outdone by Musashi.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:42.000
It's not like being blue means he's weak.

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.390
Hey, Kojiro.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.200
I need to talk to you about something.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:48.120
What is it?!

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.800
What's got you so tense?

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.420
What did you want to talk about?

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.320
Listen...

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.180
During your sword trial,

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.130
did you see anything?

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.790
See anything?

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:19.540
Like what?

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:21.800
Stuff from your past, maybe.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:25.010
No, but it happened so fast
that I'm not really sure.

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.790
I see...

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.370
What are you getting at?

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:34.350
During mine... I saw Pops.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:39.280
That dark lady showed me something.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.820
I think she might know your dad.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.860
What are you saying?

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:52.090
I'm not really sure.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.640
But she talked like they knew each other.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.800
Did Pops ever mention her?

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:00.460
No, never.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:04.750
All he left for me were the 
legends in those scrolls,

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.200
this katana,

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:10.360
and the steel horse.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.650
The steel horse...

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:20.720
These are the vehicles that people...
 that Bushi hands use, right?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:25.110
We never saw them back in our town,
 but there're a bunch here.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.610
I wonder why Pops had one.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:32.110
<i>Could it be?</i>

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:38.290
<i>Did Dad have some kind of connection 
to Bushi from outside of town?</i>

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:46.290
A middle-aged man with white hair 
and scars over his eye...

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.020
Isn't that who we're supposed to be after?

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.570
The great criminal...

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:59.270
who spirited away with the obsidian 
goddess inside of his body.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.340
Yeah.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:05.100
But if that redheaded boy
 is the goddess's host,

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.150
the description is all wrong.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:08.100
Except...

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:12.050
it's been fifteen years 
since he went into hiding.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:17.950
Suppose the goddess picked a 
different vessel for some reason.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.710
His name was Musashi, right?

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:28.580
He didn't seem to have any 
clue about the goddess.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.560
Kojiro?

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:38.120
Let's get a move on.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:44.110
The other Bushi are already 
on their way out.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:50.460
<i>Dad... I always assumed he was like me</i>

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:54.410
<i>and spent his whole life in Tatsuyama.</i>

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.560
<i>After everyone else in this country 
cast aside their pride</i>

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.030
<i>and gave up on resisting the oni,</i>

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:07.260
<i>the Bushi continued to fight 
for people's place in this world.</i>

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:11.010
<i>It's their way of life.</i>

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:14.680
<i>Kojiro... you're not trash.</i>

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:18.740
<i>You're the descendant of a proud, 
courageous bloodline.</i>

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.630
<i>Don't ever forget that.</i>

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:28.870
<i>I wish I could have talked to him more.</i>

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:42.930
<i>But... the Bushi world he always used
to talk about is in front of me now.</i>

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:49.870
<i>Maybe if I walk the same path he did, 
I'll be able to figure something out.</i>

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:12.640
Kojiro sure is taking a while...

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.590
I wonder what's up.

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:19.510
He seemed lost in thought.

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:23.360
Maybe he's sulking after seeing your sword.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:28.800
To be honest, he never seemed 
as motivated as you.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.290
Who's unmotivated about what now?

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.710
Kojiro!

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.460
Where'd you go?

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:39.340
What do you mean? 
I was getting food and supplies.

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:43.620
You two need to get us a lead 
on the next Kishin, too.

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:45.580
Well, looky there. He <i>is</i> motivated.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.190
I bought a map, too.

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.790
Hey, you really did!

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:51.550
A map? Lemme see!

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.900
So this is Hinomoto?

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.420
Wow! I've never seen 
anything like it before!

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:02.800
Man, Aki is tiny!

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.480
Hey, where's Samidare Castle?!

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:07.580
Where are we headed next?

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:08.790
I'm not sure.

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:12.960
I've never seen such a big map before.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:15.810
It's so big, I don't know where to start...

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.820
What are we going to do?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:21.570
The great eastern mine is here.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.410
Which means we're right here.

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:26.380
There are mountains to the north.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.100
That'll make the going tough.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:31.800
But if we head west, 
we'll be right back where we started.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:33.400
That being the case...

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.980
How about we head east?

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.190
Makes sense!

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.360
Sounds good!

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.770
You feeling ready now, Kojiro?

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:45.880
Yeah.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.240
I figured I needed to get my head straight 
if we're really gonna do this.

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.120
<i>That's right. We're finally 
getting started for real.</i>

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:14.110
There's a whole lot we've never seen before.

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:18.380
But I don't mind. We can go check it out...

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:22.320
Our Bushi band of three!

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:25.090
Yeah!

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:29.120
You got it, Captain!

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:52.980
All right...

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:55.080
We're headed east!

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:59.280
Time for the Kanemaki Band to move out!

